// The Biome base every TypeScript/JavaScript package in a repository's own
// `biome.json` extends — docs/canon/node.md: "Linting and formatting |
// Biome | one tool for both, so formatting is never a second opinion."
//
// Biome resolves `extends` relative to the child config, so a package's own
// config is:
//
//   { "extends": ["../lint/biome.base.jsonc"] }
//
// (or the correct relative path to wherever this repository's `lint/`
// lives). See lint/README.md for the mechanics — this file is one of a
// set of configurations a repository copies, not references, because only
// a copy commits to a schema version this repository itself pins.
//
// `formatter.lineWidth` is 109, not Biome's 80 default and not a round
// number: it is the longest line this repository's own hand-written
// TypeScript already had before Biome ever touched it (ts/src/config.test.ts,
// checked when this file was written). No single width makes an unformatted
// codebase format to itself exactly — this one already mixes single lines
// past 120 columns with calls deliberately wrapped well under 100 — but 109
// is the value that minimises the reflow: narrower re-wraps lines nobody
// asked to change, and wider re-joins calls that were wrapped on purpose.
// `organizeImports` stays OFF: this repository's own imports are not
// consistently ordered (node built-ins before or after a package, by file),
// so turning it on would be asserting a convention nobody has followed
// rather than encoding one that already holds.
{
  "$schema": "https://biomejs.dev/schemas/2.5.14/schema.json",
  "vcs": {
    "enabled": true,
    "clientKind": "git",
    "useIgnoreFile": true
  },
  "files": {
    "ignoreUnknown": false
  },
  "formatter": {
    "enabled": true,
    "indentStyle": "space",
    "indentWidth": 2,
    "lineWidth": 109
  },
  "javascript": {
    "formatter": {
      "quoteStyle": "double"
    }
  },
  "linter": {
    "enabled": true,
    "rules": {
      "preset": "recommended"
    }
  },
  "assist": {
    "enabled": true,
    "actions": {
      "source": {
        "organizeImports": "off"
      }
    }
  }
}
